WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.870
In 2025, the world moved more goods and

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:05.440
services than ever before about $35

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.260
trillion worth, a jump of roughly 7.5%.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.780
That is the surprise.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.420
Trade is not shrinking.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.340
It is growing at record speed.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.900
Containers are fuller, ports are busier,

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.900
and the value crossing borders is larger

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.640
than any year in history.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.850
So why does it feel like the trading

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.820
system is falling apart?

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.760
Because volume and trust are moving in

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:26.900
opposite directions.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.700
The same year that set the trade record

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.220
also produced new tariffs, new export

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.470
controls, and a quiet retreat from the

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.420
rules that made global trade predictable

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.890
in the first place.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.780
That is the paradox we are going to

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.200
unpack, more trade, less trust.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.440
How can both be true at the same time?

00:00:43.470 --> 00:00:45.420
Start with the record itself.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:48.140
The United Nations Trade Agency, UNCTAD,

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.120
estimates that world trade in goods and

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.060
services grew by about 7.5% in 2025,

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.850
reaching roughly $35 trillion.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.730
Manufacturing, especially electronics, did

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.340
most of the heavy lifting.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.660
Energy and cars lagged behind.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.200
But here is the second half of the

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.430
sentence, the one that usually gets left

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:07.920
out.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.270
The same agency warns that the outlook is

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.060
increasingly fragile.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.540
Growth is expected to slow sharply in

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.780
2026.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:17.740
The World Trade Organization projects

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.920
goods trade growth of under 2%, so the

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.310
record year is not a sign that all is

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:22.860
well.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:25.020
It is the last surge before the weather

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:25.720
changes.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.490
That brings us to the rule that made this

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:29.850
system work, a phrase worth knowing, most

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:31.440
favored nation treatment.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.140
It sounds grand, but the idea is simple.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.080
When a country gives one trading partner

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.330
its best tariff rate, it must give the

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:39.820
same rate to everyone.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.980
No favorites, one price for all.

00:01:42.010 --> 00:01:43.760
That single promise is what kept the

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.040
global system from collapsing into a web

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.240
of private deals.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.580
The WTO says the share of world trade

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:51.190
actually conducted on those most favored

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.520
nation terms has fallen to about 72%, and

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.100
is still declining.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.320
That number matters.

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.530
It means roughly a quarter of global trade

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.020
is now happening outside the old rulebook,

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.820
under regional deals, special exemptions,

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:07.270
tariffs aimed at specific countries, or no

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.410
clear rule at all.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.800
Now here is where the paradox sharpens.

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.160
If trust is falling, why is volume still

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:13.940
rising?

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.890
The short answer, because the world is not

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:16.590
decoupling.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:17.870
It is rerouting.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:19.610
Think of the trade map as a highway

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:20.200
system.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.900
The roads are not disappearing.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.120
They are being redrawn.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.500
Cars are taking different exits.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.880
The clearest example is North America.

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:30.220
For decades, China was the United States

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.060
largest trading partner.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.700
In 2026, Mexico overtook it.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:36.970
Mexico's exports to the United States now

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:41.260
top those from China, about $475 billion

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.820
versus roughly $427 billion.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.700
That is not a small story.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.730
It is the largest reordering of American

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.070
trade relationships in a generation.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.730
It is being driven partly by tariffs and

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:56.020
partly by companies choosing partners.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.400
They trust more than the cheapest option.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.660
The same pattern shows up across the map.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:03.460
Vietnam is pulling in more manufacturing.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.940
India is becoming an alternative assembly

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:06.460
base.

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:08.610
Taiwan's chip industry is being asked to

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:10.490
prove where its products go.

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.980
Export controls on advanced semiconductors

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.250
are rewriting which chips can cross which

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:15.880
borders.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.280
The old question was, where is it cheapest

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.010
to build?

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.200
The new question is, who is it safe to

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.100
build with?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.130
That shift has a price, and markets are

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:25.140
starting to price it.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:27.060
Companies now say they are willing to pay

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.150
10% to 25% more for supply chains built on

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.560
trust rather than on pure cost.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.900
That premium is not an abstraction.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:37.170
It shows up in inventories, in factory

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.070
locations, in margins, and eventually in

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.840
the prices consumers pay.

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.090
This is why the trade story is also a

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.240
market story.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.590
When resilience becomes a budget line, it

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:49.510
changes earnings, inflation, and

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.910
investment decisions.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:52.760
The cheapest supplier is no longer

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:54.160
automatically the winner.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.860
The trusted supplier is.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:57.660
So let us be precise about what is really

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.160
happening because the language gets muddy.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.620
This is not decoupling.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.140
Total trade between major economies is not

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.050
collapsing.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.100
The United States and China still trade

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.980
enormous volumes with each other.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:11.260
Global flows keep setting records.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.520
What is changing is the geometry.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.380
Goods are taking longer routes.

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:17.020
Suppliers are multiplying.

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.140
Inventories are being held higher, closer

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.060
to home, in more countries.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.850
Governments are building factories they

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:24.180
used to import from.

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:27.130
The World Bank, the IMF, and the WTO all

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:28.700
point the same direction.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:30.490
Trade is fragmenting into blocks that

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.250
trade more with friends and less with

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.260
everyone else.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.290
The practical consequence is a quieter,

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.540
slower, more expensive world.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.570
One where the same goods move, but with

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.630
more paperwork, more distance, and more

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.620
risk priced in.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.920
Here is the honest uncertainty, stated

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:45.660
plainly.

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:48.220
Nobody knows how far this rerouting goes.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.180
It is possible that tariffs come down,

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:52.740
negotiations succeed, and much of the old

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:53.900
system survives.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.540
It is also possible that the blocks

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.980
harden, that trust keeps falling, and that

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.400
trade keeps growing only inside smaller,

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.590
safer circles.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.870
The signal to watch is not the headline

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.340
number.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.370
It is the behavior underneath it.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.140
Watch whether companies keep building

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:09.950
factories in new countries, or start

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.020
reversing.

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:13.520
Watch whether trade agreements multiply or

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.100
stall.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:15.700
Watch whether the share of trade on most

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.910
favored nation terms keeps falling or

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:18.980
stabilizes.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.660
The map is the story now.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:22.440
Not how much the world trades, but who

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:24.550
trades with whom, along which routes under

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:25.560
which rules.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.820
Trade can grow and trust can fall at the

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.990
same time, and that is exactly what the

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:31.570
record year is telling us.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.220
The volume is real.

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.840
The trust is the part still being

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:35.820
renegotiated.

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:38.070
That is the market question for the next

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.990
phase of the global economy.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:42.190
Not whether the world keeps trading, but

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.050
whether it can learn to trust again while

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:44.660
it does.
